<Layouts.flash_group flash={@flash} />
<%!-- Roadmap shares the landing page's dark space theme, fixed regardless of
      the visitor's daisyUI preference. Built from the product backlog:
      .code_my_spec/stories/political_systems_progression_backlog.md --%>
<style>
  body { background: #05070f; }
  body > ul.menu a, body > ul.menu li { color: #cbd5e1; }
</style>

<div class="fixed inset-0 -z-10 overflow-hidden" aria-hidden="true">
  <div
    class="absolute inset-0"
    style="background:
      radial-gradient(1px 1px at 12% 22%, #e2e8f0 50%, transparent 51%),
      radial-gradient(1px 1px at 78% 12%, #cbd5e1 50%, transparent 51%),
      radial-gradient(1.5px 1.5px at 55% 38%, #f1f5f9 50%, transparent 51%),
      radial-gradient(1px 1px at 33% 68%, #cbd5e1 50%, transparent 51%),
      radial-gradient(1px 1px at 88% 55%, #e2e8f0 50%, transparent 51%),
      radial-gradient(1.5px 1.5px at 8% 85%, #f1f5f9 50%, transparent 51%),
      radial-gradient(1px 1px at 65% 82%, #cbd5e1 50%, transparent 51%),
      radial-gradient(1px 1px at 45% 8%, #e2e8f0 50%, transparent 51%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, #05070f 0%, #0a1020 55%, #0b1526 100%);"
  >
  </div>
</div>

<div class="relative z-[1] mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 pb-24 pt-8">
  <%!-- Top bar --%>
  <nav class="flex items-center justify-between">
    <.link href={~p"/"} class="text-sm font-black tracking-tight text-slate-200 hover:text-white">
      Broken Oaths
    </.link>
    <.link
      href={~p"/play"}
      class="rounded-lg bg-amber-500 px-5 py-2 text-sm font-bold text-slate-950 transition hover:bg-amber-400"
    >
      Play free
    </.link>
  </nav>

  <%!-- Hero --%>
  <header class="mt-16 text-center">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-amber-400/90">
      Roadmap
    </p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-100 sm:text-6xl">
      From Stone Age tribes to intergalactic gods
    </h1>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-300">
      Broken Oaths marches through the whole span of history and then past it.
      Every age hands you a new way to relate to the players you beat and the
      players you befriend. The through line runs from brutal extraction toward
      voluntary cooperation, and each cooperative tier unlocks something bigger
      that no single power can build alone.
    </p>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
      An autonomous development harness builds this in public, tier by tier.
      What ships stays free to play.
    </p>
  </header>

  <%!-- Legend --%>
  <div class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-4 text-xs text-slate-400">
    <span class="flex items-center gap-2">
      <span class="inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-400"></span> Playable now
    </span>
    <span class="flex items-center gap-2">
      <span class="inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-amber-400"></span> Building next
    </span>
    <span class="flex items-center gap-2">
      <span class="inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-sky-400"></span> Planned
    </span>
    <span class="flex items-center gap-2">
      <span class="inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-fuchsia-400"></span> Vision
    </span>
  </div>

  <%!-- Playable now --%>
  <section class="mt-16">
    <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-slate-500">
      Playable now
    </h2>
    <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/30 bg-slate-900/60 p-5 backdrop-blur">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-100">The living planet</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
          A seamless hex globe of nearly thirty thousand tiles ticks once a
          minute, forever. You explore under real fog of war, found cities,
          research the early tech tree, and fight barbarians and rivals for the
          ground worth holding.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/30 bg-slate-900/60 p-5 backdrop-blur">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-100">Conquer into vassalage</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
          Take a rival's last city and they swear fealty instead of leaving the
          game. They keep playing as your vassal, pay tribute, answer your
          call to arms, and hand you their honor and their grudge.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/30 bg-slate-900/60 p-5 backdrop-blur">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-100">Oaths that strain</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
          Heavy tribute and a dishonorable lord raise a vassal's oath strain in
          plain sight. Treat your vassals well and they hold. Squeeze them and
          the pressure builds toward a break.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/30 bg-slate-900/60 p-5 backdrop-blur">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-100">Rebellion and independence</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
          Vassals conspire in secret through a shared pact, rise together, and
          fight a real war of independence. Hold your freed cities long enough
          and the oath breaks for good.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%!-- The political ladder --%>
  <section class="mt-20">
    <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-slate-500">
      The political ladder
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-300">
      As you advance through the ages, your options for ruling the players you
      defeat change with you. Each tier trades away raw extraction for stability
      and scale, so players migrate toward the newer systems the way real
      societies did. The tool that applies depends on your age and the gap
      between you and the other player.
    </p>

    <ol class="mt-8 space-y-3">
      <li class="flex gap-4 rounded-xl border border-sky-500/25 bg-slate-900/50 p-5 backdrop-blur">
        <span class="mt-1 text-lg font-black text-slate-600">01</span>
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-100">Raiding</h3>
            <span class="rounded-full bg-sky-400/15 px-2 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-sky-300">Stone Age · Planned</span>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
            The tribal phase. Break a city's defenses, take spoils of gold and
            production, and leave. The owner keeps the city and no bond forms.
            Peers raid peers, and nobody rules anybody yet.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="flex gap-4 rounded-xl border border-sky-500/25 bg-slate-900/50 p-5 backdrop-blur">
        <span class="mt-1 text-lg font-black text-slate-600">02</span>
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-100">Conquest</h3>
            <span class="rounded-full bg-sky-400/15 px-2 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-sky-300">Bronze Age · Planned</span>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
            Hold individual cities by force and squeeze heavy tribute from them.
            Keep a garrison moving through each hold or watch it slip away.
            Conquest works, but it scales badly on purpose.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="flex gap-4 rounded-xl border border-sky-500/25 bg-slate-900/50 p-5 backdrop-blur">
        <span class="mt-1 text-lg font-black text-slate-600">03</span>
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-100">Administration</h3>
            <span class="rounded-full bg-sky-400/15 px-2 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-sky-300">Iron Age · Planned</span>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
            Appoint a governor who lightens the burden on the conquered in
            exchange for less extraction, and settle wars through negotiation
            instead of endless garrisoning. The bureaucratic answer to an empire
            that grew too wide to hold by hand.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="flex gap-4 rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/40 bg-slate-900/60 p-5 backdrop-blur">
        <span class="mt-1 text-lg font-black text-emerald-500/70">04</span>
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-100">Vassalage</h3>
            <span class="rounded-full bg-emerald-400/15 px-2 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-emerald-300">Feudal Age · Playable now</span>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
            A contract, not a cage. Vassals keep full control of their lands,
            pay moderate tribute, and answer commands they can refuse at a cost.
            Treat them well and hold many. Mistreat them and they rebel, or a
            rival lord poaches them with a better deal.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="flex gap-4 rounded-xl border border-fuchsia-500/25 bg-slate-900/50 p-5 backdrop-blur">
        <span class="mt-1 text-lg font-black text-slate-600">05</span>
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-100">Colonialism</h3>
            <span class="rounded-full bg-fuchsia-400/15 px-2 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-fuchsia-300">Vision</span>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
            When you defeat a player two or more ages behind, you cannot simply
            crush them. You appoint a viceroy, collect moderate tribute, and send
            technology down the ladder. The colony keeps full autonomy and grows
            toward parity, then matures into a vassal as the gap closes.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="flex gap-4 rounded-xl border border-fuchsia-500/25 bg-slate-900/50 p-5 backdrop-blur">
        <span class="mt-1 text-lg font-black text-slate-600">06</span>
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-100">Federalism</h3>
            <span class="rounded-full bg-fuchsia-400/15 px-2 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-fuchsia-300">Vision</span>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
            Near equals pool their strength into a voluntary union with no
            tribute between members. Federations wage unified war and take on
            mega projects that no single power can afford, up to space programs.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="flex gap-4 rounded-xl border border-fuchsia-500/25 bg-slate-900/50 p-5 backdrop-blur">
        <span class="mt-1 text-lg font-black text-slate-600">07</span>
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-100">Hegemony</h3>
            <span class="rounded-full bg-fuchsia-400/15 px-2 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-fuchsia-300">Vision</span>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
            The top of the cooperation ladder. A hegemon leads by consent rather
            than rule, with no tribute and no direct control, and rallies allied
            powers into the largest undertakings the game can produce.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <%!-- The long arc --%>
  <section class="mt-20">
    <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-slate-500">
      The long arc, to the stars
    </h2>
    <div class="mt-6 space-y-4">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-fuchsia-500/25 bg-slate-900/50 p-5 backdrop-blur">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-100">A tech tree that reaches the space age</h3>
          <span class="rounded-full bg-fuchsia-400/15 px-2 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-fuchsia-300">Vision</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
          The tree runs the full length of history and keeps going. Past the
          modern era it opens into a Master of Orion style intergalactic 4X, so
          the same civilization you founded on a grassland hex eventually leaves
          its home world and settles the stars.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-fuchsia-500/25 bg-slate-900/50 p-5 backdrop-blur">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-100">Colonize the newcomers</h3>
          <span class="rounded-full bg-fuchsia-400/15 px-2 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-fuchsia-300">Vision</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
          The world never ends, so fresh players keep arriving on younger worlds
          far behind the old powers. The age gap turns those first contacts into
          colonial relationships, where the advanced lift the young toward
          parity while drawing tribute from the frontier.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-fuchsia-500/25 bg-slate-900/50 p-5 backdrop-blur">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-100">Build the impossible together</h3>
          <span class="rounded-full bg-fuchsia-400/15 px-2 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-fuchsia-300">Vision</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
          At the far end, cooperation beats domination. Federations and hegemonies
          pool whole civilizations into intergalactic mega projects that no lone
          empire could ever complete.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%!-- The god layer --%>
  <section class="mt-20">
    <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-slate-500">
      The god layer
    </h2>
    <div class="mt-6 rounded-xl border border-fuchsia-500/25 bg-slate-900/50 p-6 backdrop-blur">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-100">Gods above the board</h3>
        <span class="rounded-full bg-fuchsia-400/15 px-2 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-fuchsia-300">Vision</span>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
        Some players join not as rulers but as gods. A god strikes bargains with
        the rulers below, granting a miracle or a won war in exchange for a temple
        and worship. As the game reaches the stars, so do the gods, and the deals
        they broker scale to intergalactic stakes.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%!-- Close --%>
  <section class="mt-20 text-center">
    <p class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-300">
      The Stone Age loop is playable today. Everything above ships in order, in
      public, and stays free.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6 flex flex-col items-center gap-2">
      <.link
        href={~p"/play"}
        class="rounded-lg bg-amber-500 px-10 py-4 text-lg font-bold text-slate-950 shadow-lg shadow-amber-500/25 transition hover:bg-amber-400"
      >
        Play free
      </.link>
      <.link href={~p"/"} class="text-sm text-slate-400 underline-offset-4 hover:text-slate-200 hover:underline">
        Back to home
      </.link>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
